WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.130
- [Presenter] Do you ever
look at cake decorating

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:03.650
on Instagram and think,
"God, I could never do that."

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:05.170
Well, guess what, yes you can.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.060
Buying a professionally decorated cake

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.290
can cost hundreds of
dollars, it doesn't take

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.400
that much extra effort or talent

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.060
to decorate your own cake at home.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.615
We're gonna teach you five
really easy decorating styles

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.560
to zhuzh up your next cake.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.270
Honestly, like cake, it's
a really tangible way

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.720
to show people you love them.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.240
First things first, we have to prep

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.180
our cakes to be decorated.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.850
Get a little icing, secure
the board on top of that,

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.530
and start building our cakes.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.950
All you really need to do is plop

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.070
a good amount of icing down first,

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.350
more than you think, honestly.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:36.860
You don't have to worry
about it being perfect,

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.180
you could pipe it on if you wanted,

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.844
but I dunno, it's not really
the biggest deal in the world.

00:00:40.844 --> 00:00:42.710
And then, for the top
layer, you're actually

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.130
gonna put it bottom side down,

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.880
that's a lot flatter and we want

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.640
a really sharp edge to our cake.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.230
You might have to move it a little bit

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.520
to make sure that it's
totally level on all sides,

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.410
and then put a whole
bunch of frosting on top.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.440
I like to take the back of my spatula

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.533
and just dab the icing onto the cake.

00:00:59.965 --> 00:01:01.326
And then you're gonna
use the offset spatula

00:01:01.326 --> 00:01:04.634
to flatten out the sides,
and get off any excess icing.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.360
This is your primer, if
you will, on your cake

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.150
to ensure that the finished coat

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.030
is gonna go on really nice and smooth.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:12.150
As you can see, there's crumbs

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.410
that kinda get caught in the mess,

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.360
and that's why it's called a crumb coat.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.763
We're gonna chill that until
we're ready to decorate.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.970
To make this job really easy,

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.270
all you need is a piping bag, a spoon,

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.140
an offset spatula, you know I love 'em,

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.960
a cake board, and a rotating
cake stand, if possible.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.894
Lastly, you'll need a rosette piping tip.

00:01:28.894 --> 00:01:31.090
Not all of these tools are necessary,

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.170
I mean really all you need
is a piping bag and a tip,

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:35.040
but they make the job a lot easier.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.900
First things first, we're
gonna put the piping tip

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.620
into the bag, then turn it right around

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:41.174
and put the bag over
your non-dominant hand

00:01:41.174 --> 00:01:43.686
with the top of the bag kinda folded down.

00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:45.530
And you're gonna use your thumb, actually,

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:47.880
to help scrape off the extra icing.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.560
Put the top back up and squeeze it

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.980
in-between your thumb and your hand,

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:51.830
and that's where you're gonna have

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:54.120
all the pressure coming out of.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:56.310
So, a lot of people want to press down

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:57.530
in the middle of the bag, and it

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:58.840
actually gives a lot of uneven pressure,

00:01:58.840 --> 00:01:59.770
and that's not what you want to do.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:02.050
It's actually a lot harder, as well.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:03.000
So, when you're making your rosette

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.050
you start in the middle,
apply even pressure

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.460
until the end, and just
curve around really easy

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.430
and at the very end, when you're trying to

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.000
make the edge of your rosette,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.620
you just flick your wrist a little bit,

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.610
wrap it around, and release that pressure.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.760
You just kind of quickly
dismount, if you will.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.330
Oh, dismount, that's a good word for it,

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.497
yeah, you dismount!

00:02:19.497 --> 00:02:20.810
And the first few that you do,

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.130
they're gonna feel kind of awkward,

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:23.805
you're gonna have some that
look better than others,

00:02:23.805 --> 00:02:26.440
but I will say just go for it.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.440
To fill in those holes that
are naturally gonna be there,

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.880
all you need to do is just
put the tip down in that hole,

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.130
apply a little bit of pressure,

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.760
and then kind of flick your wrist

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.060
so it almost looks like
it's part of a petal

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.410
of a nearby rosette.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:38.860
The reason why the rosette cake is great

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.125
is you really don't need to be perfect,

00:02:40.125 --> 00:02:43.360
it looks so cool when it's done.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.640
It's so elegant, it's really, really easy,

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.805
it's just one piping tip
with one icing color,

00:02:47.805 --> 00:02:49.490
next thing you know, it looks like

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:51.140
you've been doing this for years.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.580
So, to start the ombre cake,

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.500
you're gonna take the darkest color

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.210
and pipe it around the bottom.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:02.670
Put two thick layers
of icing on the bottom

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.510
and then do two stripes of the next color.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.010
Just choose whatever colors you want,

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.580
you could do from a dark blue

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.224
all the way to a really,
really light blue.

00:03:10.224 --> 00:03:12.200
We're going for more of a sunrise look,

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.420
like a tequila sunrise is
what we're calling this cake.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.130
I'm gonna top it with white, it's gonna be

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.260
a really nice gradient of colors.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.410
This tool is a bench
scraper or a dough cutter.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.640
You can drag it right along
the bottom of the stand itself

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.240
so it'll be really, really level.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.270
If you want a really clean
stripe you can start here,

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.430
but we were going for
that gradient ombre look

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.070
so now we're gonna use
that excess frosting

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:33.230
and go up, go down, go in
a few different directions

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.250
so that you're really getting a good mix

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.883
of all of the colors together.

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:40.683
The fun thing about this is, honestly,

00:03:40.683 --> 00:03:42.864
anyone can do it, it's so easy,

00:03:42.864 --> 00:03:44.750
and you really just have
to know when to stop,

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:45.910
like, that's usually my problem

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.030
is that I just want to go and go

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.580
and I have more fun with it.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.630
We're just topping it with a little bit

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:53.910
of crushed Graham Cracker and
an umbrella, because we can.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:55.180
Just play with it, that's the fun thing

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.790
about decorating cakes is
they can be kind of kitschy

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:00.360
or elegant, or whatever
you want them to be.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.770
I think we really just need a vacation,

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.400
that might be why we went with the sunset.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.330
We're gonna show you how to make

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.340
homemade buttercream succulents.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:10.380
And for dyeing your frosting
we recommend using gel colors,

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.110
they're just a little bit more saturated.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:17.050
We're going for kind of a dark
greenish-gray kind of color.

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.390
I'm using some green,
a little bit of brown,

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:21.270
and a little bit of blue.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.700
A little goes a long way,
so start with a little

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:24.990
and you can always add more.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.210
Alright, so I've got the green,

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:27.330
I'm also gonna use a little bit of pink

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.470
for these succulents, and so this is,

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:30.870
I don't know, what tip is this?

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.774
Oh yeah, it's a petal
nozzle, yep, that's it.

00:04:32.774 --> 00:04:35.400
This one's great for making
roses and succulents.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.300
And what we're gonna do is put

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.550
a stripe of pink down one side of the bag.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:41.310
And, similar to the ombre cake,

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:42.350
it doesn't have to be perfect,

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.930
just get it in there
from right to the start

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.790
of the piping tip, all the
way to the top of the bag.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:51.170
And we're gonna fill in the
rest with the green color.

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:52.690
And again, I'm gonna use my thumb, here,

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:56.070
to scrape off the icing
when it gets into the bag.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:58.560
We're gonna twist, make
sure there's no air bubbles,

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.980
and set that aside while you
grab some parchment paper.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:03.380
So, just a little square
is what we're gonna use

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.130
to make our succulents on.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.610
And you're gonna just test the icing

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:09.140
to make sure that the color is coming out

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.460
the way that you want it to.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:12.290
Kind of schmoop schmoop, get it out there

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.840
until I'm happy with the color.

00:05:14.686 --> 00:05:15.790
A new piece of parchment, and I'm gonna

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.700
make a mound of icing in the middle and

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.573
then do an X shape over that.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.330
And then you're gonna do little C shapes

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.670
all around that X that you made.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:28.170
Do a quarter turn in-between each one.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:29.907
When you're trying to dismount that icing

00:05:29.907 --> 00:05:34.000
I think it's better to go down
into the parchment itself.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:34.910
And then just keep going until

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.983
you're happy with the
size of that succulent.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.220
With the same nozzle you can play with it

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.440
and create different shapes.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.670
So you're gonna turn the bag to ensure

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.220
that the pink side's kind of on the top

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:45.470
of the nozzle when it's coming out,

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:47.360
and you're gonna go in a loop motion,

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.740
turning your parchment around

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.890
and going in these
little loop, loop, loops

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:52.360
until you're all the way around.

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:54.726
And just keep going up
until you have a beautiful,

00:05:54.726 --> 00:05:57.468
unique little cactus, like this.

00:05:57.468 --> 00:05:58.930
You can just buy a beginner's piping set,

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.446
all of the tips we used here are

00:06:00.446 --> 00:06:02.540
kind of the standard
ones that come in there.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:03.980
If you're nervous about
spending much money

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:06.110
on frosting, and you still
want to practice your piping,

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.566
in culinary school they used to have us

00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:09.700
buy powdered instant mash potatoes

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:10.750
and practice with that.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:11.977
Top tip, you heard it here first,

00:06:11.977 --> 00:06:13.880
don't take it too
seriously,1 just have fun!

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.250
And then, while those are
chilling in the fridge,

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:16.640
we're gonna assemble our naked cake.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.330
So this one's really cool and it looks

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:20.860
really elegant and is
ridiculously easy to do.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.640
Similar to our crumb
coat, you're gonna take

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.740
a bench scraper and
scrape off all the excess.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.262
You're gonna really push into the cake

00:06:27.262 --> 00:06:29.640
and get as much icing off as you can.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:31.420
So it's gonna look, you know, naked.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.370
They're very trendy right now, very in.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.400
And then you can start
putting on your succulents.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:37.840
So these came straight out of the freezer,

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.400
so that they're really easy to work with.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.343
It looks very intimidating, and you

00:06:40.343 --> 00:06:42.300
may not want to try it because you think

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.440
people will think your piping's not good,

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:46.350
but the point of this
and why it's so great,

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:48.280
is that there's so much on there

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.910
and it's just like an
overwhelming, beautiful, gorgeous,

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.730
unique cake that you don't see everywhere,

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:55.210
and you should just go ahead and try it.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:58.040
Now, for the drip cake,
very dramatic and elegant,

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.449
and also very on trend.

00:06:59.449 --> 00:07:01.830
You make a really simple
white chocolate ganache

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.020
and then dyed it this
really gorgeous blue color.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.580
You pour the ganache in
fourths along the cake.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:08.707
So the cake's really
cold, the ganache is warm,

00:07:08.707 --> 00:07:11.758
and I'm pouring the warm
ganache onto the cold cake,

00:07:11.758 --> 00:07:13.686
it's gonna kind of set as it goes.

00:07:13.686 --> 00:07:15.400
I'm just gonna use a dinner spoon

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.100
and kind of coax the
ganache in the direction

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.210
that I want, to make sure that

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:21.550
it's pooling down the side of the cake.

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:24.010
You could use a piping bag
or a little squeeze bottle

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:26.080
to do this, but we thought
this is a really organic,

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.907
natural way, as well as not really needing

00:07:27.907 --> 00:07:29.430
a ton of extra equipment.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:30.280
You could top it with anything,

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:32.810
candy, macarons, or just leave it plain,

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:35.963
it looks really gorgeous with
a clean, shiny top, as well.

00:07:43.534 --> 00:07:46.070
Mirror glaze is an absolute show stopper,

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.420
do not be intimidated, you can do this.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:49.620
You just have to be prepared,

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:50.550
so make sure you have all your

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:51.810
mise en place ready, because you do

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:53.210
have to work quickly with this glaze.

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:55.200
To make sure that it's
really, really well mixed,

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.700
we recommend using a stick blender.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.060
If you put cling film on the top

00:07:58.060 --> 00:07:59.830
that can help get rid
of any extra bubbles,

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.130
but as you can see some remain

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:03.090
so you want to get out as many as you can.

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:05.130
The ideal temperature
to pour the mirror glaze

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.810
on top of the cake is anywhere between

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:09.050
90 to 96 degrees fahrenheit.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.350
The most important things about

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:11.610
doing a mirror glaze is one,

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:13.530
making sure that it's frozen solid,

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:14.610
and two, making sure that it's

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:16.300
as smooth as you can possibly get it.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.230
The glaze is warm when
you're pouring it on,

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.260
so the cold cake will help the glaze set

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.560
really nicely on the cake.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:30.330
Take an offset spatula
and do a little schmoop!

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:33.150
And then it really
completes that marble look.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.270
And this is the fun part, it's when

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:35.580
all of the hard work pays off

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:36.470
and you just get to watch this

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:38.173
mesmerizing process take shape.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:41.760
'Cause we just can't help ourselves

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:42.840
we just had to add a little bit

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:44.986
of silver leaf to the top as well.

00:08:44.986 --> 00:08:47.400
Most of it will drip off, but
you just want to make sure

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.530
that you're getting a good
mix of the two colors.

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:50.363
Hello!

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:54.260
Oh my god, that's so cool!

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.810
Every occasion, every party, has a cake,

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.770
and this is just a few helpful tips

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.420
to help you make yours really stand out

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.260
at your next event.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:12.240
So all the care, all the effort,

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.810
all the fun creativity that
goes into making these cakes,

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:16.000
don't be afraid to eat them in the end,

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:16.900
that's the whole point,

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:18.480
that they're something great to look at

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:19.950
but also something great to eat

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.070
and enjoy with your loved ones.

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:24.670
Really though, what are
all those damn tips called?

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:25.503
- [Man] Tips!

00:09:25.503 --> 00:09:26.860
